{"repositoryId":1136217542,"availability":"available","full":"NEWSLabNTU/nano-ros","name":"nano-ros","description":"no_std ROS 2 client for microcontrollers and RTOS (Zephyr, FreeRTOS, NuttX, ThreadX) and Linux. Rust-first with C/C++ APIs; pluggable Zenoh / XRCE-DDS / Cyclone DDS backends; interoperates with standard ROS 2.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":16,"forks":3,"created":"2026-01-17T09:32:50Z","updated":"2026-10-15T14:50:02Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://newslabntu.github.io/nano-ros-book/","topics":["cortex-m","cyclonedds","dds","embedded","esp32","freertos","micro-ros","microcontroller","middleware","no-std","nuttx","real-time","riscv","robotics","ros2","rtos","rust","threadx","zenoh","zephyr"],"demo":"https://newslabntu.github.io/nano-ros-book/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:19.829Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:19.829Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:19.829Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T15:01:19.829Z","stars":16,"forks":3}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A nostd ROS 2 client library for bare-metal and RTOS targets, written in Rust. Built on zenoh-pico for lightweight pub/sub, services, and actions over TCP, serial, or raw Ethernet.","nano-ros runs directly on microcontrollers without an OS, on RTOS kernels (Zephyr, FreeRTOS, NuttX, ThreadX), and on Linux — using the same API. It interoperates with standard ROS 2 nodes via the rmwzenoh protocol. QEMU emulation is provided for Cortex-M3 (bare-metal + FreeRTOS MPS2-AN385), NuttX (ARM virt + RISC-V rv-virt), and ThreadX RISC-V64, plus a ThreadX Linux simulator — enabling full integration testing without hardware.","The project integrates formal verification (Kani bounded model checking, CBMC for the C API) and WCET measurement (DWT cycle counters, static stack analysis) into the build pipeline, providing a foundation for schedulability analysis in safety-critical systems."],"features":["Bare-metal and RTOS: runs on Cortex-M3 and STM32F4 bare-metal and on Zephyr, FreeRTOS, NuttX, and ThreadX kernels; no heap allocator required on bare-metal","ROS 2 interoperability: communicates with ROS 2 Humble nodes via rmwzenoh","QEMU emulation: Cortex-M3 (MPS2-AN385, bare-metal + FreeRTOS), NuttX (ARM virt + RISC-V rv-virt), and ThreadX RISC-V64 targets — plus the ThreadX Linux simulator — with TAP networking for CI","Customizable platform/transport: swap platform crates (clock, heap, RNG) and transport crates (TCP via smoltcp, serial, raw Ethernet) independently","Formal verification ready: Kani proofs for panic-freedom, CBMC harnesses for C API pointer safety, DWT cycle counting for WCET baselines"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NEWSLabNTU/nano-ros/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1b45af186e9f6958f011853aa7186a6b29b515cf34c030412df5a7d7aef782cb","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:20.306Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:20.306Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A nostd ROS 2 client library for bare-metal and RTOS targets, written in Rust. Built on zenoh-pico for lightweight pub/sub, services, and actions over TCP, serial, or raw Ethernet.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NEWSLabNTU/nano-ros/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"1b45af186e9f6958f011853aa7186a6b29b515cf34c030412df5a7d7aef782cb","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NEWSLabNTU/nano-ros/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:20.306Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-15T14:50:02Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NEWSLabNTU/nano-ros/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:20.307Z","hash":"1b45af186e9f6958f011853aa7186a6b29b515cf34c030412df5a7d7aef782cb","originalBytes":12559,"storedBytes":12559,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["nros","rmw","build","ros","talker","complete","linux","zenoh","rust","board","book","src","api","docs","nano-ros","zephyr","c